ifferent because humans  don't all want the same things and  neither do the tricelerans and that is  where the character yawinji comes into  play and she can almost be viewed as the  villain of this first book in the series  so like i said humanity sent messages  out friendly messages in vague  directions  and eventually  they got a message back  and it was a very simple  message  it said do not answer  do not  answer  and that was followed up by a second  message  this world has received your message  i am a pacifist in this world  it is the luck of your civilization that  i am the first to receive your message  i am warning you  do not answer do not answer do not  answer  there are tens of millions of stars in  your direction as long as you do not  answer this world will not be able to  ascertain the source of your  transmission  but if you do answer  the source will be located right away  your planet will be invaded your world  will be conquered  do not answer  do not answer  do not answer  now to understand how the character  yawinji responded when she received this  message you have to understand that this  is a character who feels betrayed by  humanity she feels wronged by humanity  she's suffered great injustices her  father was taken away from her and she  just feels as though  the world  is in a good place under the rule of  humanity she has such disdain for  humanity and really just like no hope  in the human race  so it's a twisted  turn of fate that she was the one to  first receive this message because  although  the listener who sent this message all  the way from tri solaris  back to earth  told her not to answer do not answer  clearly do not respond because that will  give away your location she responded  and her message was  also very simple  come here  i will help you conquer this world  our civilization is no longer capable of  solving its own problems  we need your force to intervene  and so yaowinji  over the course of decades  while the majority of the world has no  idea that these aliens are even on their  way  has actually been developing this  organization called eto earth trisolaris  organization and they've been helping  the tricelerians do their bidding on  earth so as i said earlier if your  question is why they chose us they  didn't choose us we chose them because  humanity is not one homogenous group if  aliens were coming you can pretty much  guarantee there would be some humans  that would be on the side of the aliens  because there's always some humans that  have weird opinions about stuff  so  try solaris  when presented with this world that's  only four light years away and they  don't need to bother terraforming it or  anything  and they've even got supporters on earth  they said yeah we're gonna go and we're  gonna send ships to earth and we're  gonna conquer them because their planet  has three sons and it's very chaotic  they've evolved to survive but they're  surviving but they're not living and  because they are an intelligent species  they kind of intuitively know that there  can be more there can be a better life  and earth to them looks like an absolute  paradise because it is and humans often  take for granted the fact that we live  on basically a paradise world  so this series isn't just depicting a  war between humans and aliens it's  depicting a war between the differing  societal values of the human race  what is good what is bad what is right  what is wrong what is the best for  humanity moving forward should humanity  even move forward at all these books are  about the battle for the very soul  of the human race the very essence of  humanity who are we in the end  what is left when it's all over when the  solar system has faded into dust  and the sun has gone out what is left  what is our legacy  and that's pretty much why the series is  called the remembrance of earth's past i  think because those are pretty heavy  themes especially in the last book  that's sinned so i think that pretty  much answers the question  in as concise a manner as i possibly can  so i hope you guys  like and subscribe for more quinn's  ideas if you're interested in science  fiction books hit up my channel it's the  place to be thanks guys  [Music]  foreign

